WEBVTT

00:18:26.996 --> 00:18:30.621
ruthless free thinkers, but they
applied it to their own work,

00:18:30.829 --> 00:18:33.163
probably even more so than they
did to each other's work.

00:18:33.579 --> 00:18:37.371
And so one would not even bring
a script or a joke to

00:18:37.371 --> 00:18:41.538
the other until he had thought it was,
you know, really good. Mm hmm.

00:18:41.538 --> 00:18:44.871
And I can see how those kinds of norms
could be really effective in partnerships.

00:18:45.579 --> 00:18:47.913
I've also seen examples, though, where,
you know,

00:18:47.913 --> 00:18:52.288
one person is basically the kind
of a creative dreamer and

00:18:52.288 --> 00:18:54.621
the other person is the really
critical evaluator.

00:18:55.371 --> 00:18:57.621
And so, you know, the first
person does the thinking,

00:18:57.621 --> 00:18:59.079
the second does the rethinking,

00:18:59.079 --> 00:19:02.579
and then it ends up being kind of
this beautiful symphony. Mm hmm.